VignetteBuilder: knitr
Description: Drop-in function-compatible R interface to the BioGeoBEARS historical biogeography framework powered by RustBEARS, a self-contained, memory-safe Rust computational engine (zero external Fortran/C++ package compilation required). Named 'RustBEARS' to preserve the upstream 'BioGeoBEARS' package namespace while keeping all modelling, optimization, stochastic mapping, and plotting function signatures 100% compatible. Original foundational methodology and R modelling framework by Nicholas J. Matzke (2013, 2014). As a matter of scholarly credit, users publishing results are requested to cite both the foundational Matzke (2013, 2014) publications and RustBEARS; run citation("RustBEARS") for complete co-citation entries. Derivative technical support and compilation issues should be reported to the GitHub issue tracker below rather than the original upstream author.
URL: https://github.com/Jhe1004/RustBEARS, http://phylo.wikidot.com/biogeobears
BugReports: https://github.com/Jhe1004/RustBEARS/issues
